#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Send read-only briefs as one Message Batch, paid by an API key, at half price.

  credit-batch submit --brief FILE [--brief FILE ...] [--shared FILE] --max-tokens N
                      [--model sonnet] [--role NAME]
  credit-batch status ID
  credit-batch results ID --dir DIR
  credit-batch --self-test

For work with no tool loop (retro digests, ticket shaping, spec review). Each brief is one
request, with the custom_id taken from its file name. A batch can take up to a day.
--shared is one stable text block sent first in every request with a cache breakpoint
(ttl 1h), for text the briefs have in common.

submit starts only when all of these hold:
  LEAN_CREDIT_RUNS=on, LEAN_CREDIT_BATCH=on   both switches, default off
  LEAN_CREDIT_TOTAL_USD=N                     the total cap shared with credit-run
  the key is in the keychain                  same item and rules as credit-run
status and results need only the key, so a paid batch can always be collected.

Cap: submit reserves the estimated cost in ~/.lean/credit-runs.jsonl before it sends
anything, under the same lock and total as credit-run. The estimate is the input tokens
(UTF-8 bytes divided by 2, rounded up) plus max_tokens for every request, at the batch
rates (50% of the prices in lib/leanstats.py, the shared text at the 1 hour cache write
rate). Refused with exit 2 when spent plus reserved plus the estimate passes the total.
A batch with no results call stays reserved. results works out the real cost from each
request's token counts at the batch rates, writes the final line and so closes the
reservation. That cost is computed, not a billed figure. The Console workspace spend
limit is the only hard limit.

results writes DIR/CUSTOM_ID.txt for every request: the text, or the error, expired or
canceled state. It refuses with one line if the batch has not ended, and exits 1 naming
every request that did not succeed.

The model is sonnet, opus, haiku or one of claude-sonnet-5-5, claude-opus-5-5, claude-haiku-5-5. Thinking and effort are left at
the model default. The call goes through credit-batch-worker.mjs and @anthropic-ai/sdk,
installed by credit-run --setup. Python standard library only.
"""
